From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: snap a window by dragging it to the screen's edge

Dragging a window to the left or right edge of its monitor snaps it to
that half, to the top edge maximizes it, as on Windows 10; while the
pointer is at an edge an outline shows where the window will go (a
window region frame, beneath the window being dragged -- no compositing
needed). Only moves snap, not resizes. Built on the move/size WinEvents
(0073), in explorer's shellkeys.c beside Win+Left/Right.

Gate: test/shellkeys-gate.sh (the preview while held at the edge, the
half on release, the top edge).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/shellkeys.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/shellkeys.c
@@ -6,7 +6,10 @@
  * File Explorer, Win+R Run, Win+I settings (the Control Panel), Win+Pause
  * System, Win+X the quick-link menu; Win+Left/Right snap the active window
  * to half the screen, Win+Up maximizes it, Win+Down restores or minimizes it.
- * The virtual desktop keys are in vdesktop.c.
+ * Dragging a window to the left or right edge snaps it to that half, to the
+ * top edge maximizes it, with an outline of where it will go (Aero Snap),
+ * on the move/size WinEvents win32u sends. The virtual desktop keys are in
+ * vdesktop.c.
